#use(std/code)
#use(std/table)

#section{Tables}::

#code{#use(std/table)} provides #code{#table} / #code{#row} / #code{#cell},
HTML-like nested cells. #code{header: n} marks the first #code{n} rows as the
header. Rows come in two spellings: nested #code{#cell} calls, or the
positional multi-body #code|{#row{a}{b}}| — one brace group per cell. They
mix freely, and cells hold arbitrary markup.

#code(lang: "plain")
	#table(header: 1)
		#row
			#cell: Name
			#cell: Role
		#row{#emph{Kiril}}{infra}

Live:

#table(header: 1)
	#row
		#cell: Name
		#cell: Role
	#row{#emph{Kiril}}{infra}

Corner cases:

#list
	#item: Without #code{header:} there is no #code{<thead>}; all rows are body rows.
	#item: A positional #code|{#row{a}{b}}| wraps each body in a plain cell; use nested #code{#cell} when a cell needs its own block content.
	#item: For source-beautiful plain-text tables see the pipe-tables page — a separate, deliberately dumb plugin.
